course: dictionary
lesson: 4007
title: Garbage, rubbish or nonsense?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can mean different things, and the words around it tell you which meaning to use. «Take out the garbage» is about bags of rubbish, but «That film was garbage» is about a film that was very bad. Always check the sentence before you choose a meaning.
explain: Garbage is an American word. In the USA and Canada people take out the garbage and put it in the garbage can. In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, people say «rubbish» and «bin» instead. If you read an American book, garbage means the same thing as rubbish.
explain: Look at this sentence: «"Sanitation engineer" is a joking or puffed-up name for a rubbish or garbage collector.» The writer uses fancy words to make a rubbish collector sound grand. The clue is the word joking, so the name is not meant to be taken seriously.
fact: Garbage means rubbish, the food waste and other things you throw away.
fact: In informal talk, garbage means nonsense, things that are untrue or very bad.
fact: In computing, garbage means useless or meaningless data.
fact: «Garbage can» and «garbage truck» are American words for a bin and a bin lorry.
fact: In the UK, people say «rubbish» or «talk rubbish» where Americans say «garbage» or «talk garbage».
exercise: «Take out the garbage before dinner.» What does garbage mean here? | Nonsense and untrue talk | A type of sandwich | *Rubbish and things you throw away | A kind of computer program
exercise: Sam says, «That film was garbage.» What does he mean? | *The film was very bad | The film was about rubbish collectors | The film was the best ever made | The film had too much music
exercise: Read this: «"Sanitation engineer" is a joking or puffed-up name for a rubbish or garbage collector.» What is a sanitation engineer? | A type of garbage can | *A joking name for a rubbish collector | A computer program | A real engineer who builds bridges
test: «The garbage truck comes every Tuesday.» What is a garbage truck? | A bus for school children | *A lorry that collects rubbish | A small car for shopping | A boat for the river
test: The file was full of garbage data, so the program crashed. What does garbage data mean? | Food waste | Lovely pictures | Very large files | *Useless, meaningless data
exam: Maya's mum says, «Don't talk garbage.» What does she mean? | Don't sing in the bath | Don't go to the bin | *Don't say nonsense or things that are untrue | Don't throw food waste on the floor
